{"title":"Muskoka cranberry plunge + Hardy Lake","startsAt":"2026-10-18T09:00:00-07:00","endsAt":"2026-10-18T21:00:00-07:00","status":"ACTIVE","type":"PHYSICAL","description":"This is one for the Gram. We'll be heading Northbound to the Muskoka area for a fun day out in the beautiful Fall color season. We'll start the day by visiting Gravenhurst which is a town in the Muskoka region, here you will have free time to grab some brunch.\n\nAfter that, we'll head over to the Muskoka Lakes Farm and Winery for a popular Fall time activity. You'll be given some chest waders so you can sink into the water surrounded by millions of Cranberries - it's a great way to get those awesome images.\n\nAfter the farm, we'll make a quick stop at a local brewery, followed by Hardy Lake Provincial Park. This small Provincial Park in Muskoka is a must do for those who like hiking. While there are many trails, we'll head on the biggest and best around Hardy Lake which will serve up some good snaps. We'll gage the groups ability and pick the most suitable hike for the day.\n\nPlease email sandra@origin-travels.com for more details and to grab a spot! We will have max 15 people on this day trip.","venue":{"name":"Yorkdale TTC Passenger Pick-up","address":"5234 William R. Allen Rd, North York, ON M6A 3A1, Canada, Toronto","lat":43.725589,"lng":-79.447857,"city":"Toronto"},"fee":null,"group":"The Wanderer's Club: group trips for active travellers","image":"https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/6/2/5/6/highres_536365174.jpeg"}